# Settings, all optional for `npm run dev` (cloudflare/.dev.vars, created by
# `npm run configure`). A deployment's values live in cloudflare/.prod.vars and
# are uploaded as Worker secrets by `npm run secrets`. Keep both files private;
# Git ignores them.
#
# Deployments only: Cloudflare Access signs people in. Its team domain and the
# application's audience (AUD) tag; with these set the app trusts only Access's
# signed token. Leave them out of .dev.vars: development has no sign-in and
# answers only on this computer.
# ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN=https://your-team.cloudflareaccess.com
# ACCESS_AUD=
# The two people. Deployments need both emails: the addresses Access allows.
OWNER_NAME=You
# OWNER_EMAIL=you@example.com
PARTNER_NAME=Partner
# PARTNER_EMAIL=partner@example.com
# Phone push: a stable VAPID keypair (changing it breaks existing subscriptions)
# and a contact. Without PUSH_CONTACT, mailto:OWNER_EMAIL is used.
VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
# PUSH_CONTACT=mailto:you@example.com
# Optional shared iCloud calendar: an Apple app-specific password, never the account password.
# ICLOUD_USERNAME=
# ICLOUD_APP_PASSWORD=
# ICLOUD_CALENDAR_NAME=Household
# ICLOUD_CALENDAR_URL=
# Optional ChatGPT connection, written by `npm run ai:connect`.
# CHATGPT_HOST_ID=
# CHATGPT_MODEL_ID=
# CHATGPT_CREDENTIAL_JSON=
